This directory contains the build variant "Element Pilot": Element with the AI agent, built so that it can be
installed and run beside the official Element Desktop.

Everything that decides where the app lives differs from the official build:

- the name (element-desktop-pilot), so the installer puts it in its own directory,
- the product name (Element Pilot), so its data is in %APPDATA%\Element Pilot and its agent data in
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Element Pilot\agent instead of Element's,
- the app ID (im.riot.pilot), so Windows keeps its taskbar entry and notifications apart,
- the link protocol (io.element.pilot); it doesn't claim element:// links, which stay with Element.

Build it with this directory as the variant, from apps/desktop:

    VARIANT_PATH=pilot/build.json pnpm run build

There is no config.json here: the web app is built with apps/web/config.json, and the build has no update server,
so it never replaces itself with an official Element build.
